Priority of Interrupts

Not all interrupts are equal.

Example:

Suppose simultaneously:

Keyboard Interrupt
Disk Interrupt
Power Failure Interrupt

arrive.

Which should run first?

Usually:

Power Failure

because it is more critical.

OS uses priorities.

Nested Interrupts

Advanced Concept.

Suppose:

Keyboard Interrupt

is being handled.

Then:

Power Failure Interrupt

arrives.

OS may pause keyboard handling and process the higher-priority interrupt first.

